evidence his cash advantage is closing the advertising gap, would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Gabe Evans (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Colorado's 8th District is a pure battleground, with no partisan lean and first-term Republican Gabe Evans defending against Democrat Manny Rutinel. Evans has raised over $5 million and holds a wide cash advantage, but Rutinel benefits from roughly $3.5 million in outside support and heavy Democratic spending against the incumbent. The lone public poll, from a Republican pollster in mid-September, showed Evans ahead by two points.\n\nMost expert raters, including Cook, Inside Elections, and Sabato's, call the race a Tossup, while several others rate it Lean or Likely Democratic for a flip. Prediction markets price Rutinel's chances between 75 and 85 percent. The overall picture is a narrow Democratic edge in one of the House's most competitive seats, with real uncertainty given thin polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7882, "margin": 4.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7652, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7649, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7806, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7027, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6862, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7621, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7968, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7638, "margin": 4.3}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7725, "margin": 4.0}]}